  "id": "M",
  "title": "Masculinisation: pitch-only vs multidimensional",
  "change": "Add formant lowering, then body resonance, then narrower intonation + darker brightness, on top of a pitch drop.",
  "rationale": "Perceived masculinity depends on F0 and on formant spacing / apparent vocal-tract length, plus voice quality and intonation (e.g. Peterson & Barney 1952; Hillenbrand et al. 1995; Fitch & Giedd 1999; Pisanski et al. 2016). Lowering pitch alone is the classic 'pitched-down' sound.",
